# Surface Pro 12in diagnostic DTB

`surface-pro-12in.dtb` is the known-working Surface Pro 12in 1st Edition
device tree used solely as a live-media fallback until the selected
`linux-aarch64` package ships
`x1p42100-microsoft-sp12in.dtb`.  It is staged only when that package does
not provide its own tree; a package-provided tree is never replaced.

Provenance: copied without modification from
<https://github.com/harrisonvanderbyl/surface-pro-12-inch-linux>, commit
`ea0f07e66beea95898d96fbeb6daa472f4735af3`, path `boot/dtb`, retrieved for
the Surface live-boot investigation.  Its SHA-256 is
`d7ed4b073c7344cb0bb2c3f7d00655df60b473588a5c0364af54537dc2c672c7`.
The matching upstream source is Linux
`arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-microsoft-sp12in.dts`, SPDX GPL-2.0-only.

The source repository does not state a license for its prebuilt `boot/dtb`.
Before promoting this diagnostic fallback beyond this contribution/testing
branch, confirm that the binary is redistributable under the upstream DTS
license (or replace it with a reproducible build from the upstream source).
